$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Sharpless Asymmetric
Dihydroxylation K2CO3 (415 mg, 3 mmol.), K3Fe(CN)6 (1.18 g, 3 mmol.),
K2OsO2(OH)4 (4 mg, 0.01 mmol.), ligand (0.025 mmol.), MeSO2NH2 (95 mg, 1
mmol.) were added to a vigorous magnetically stirred solution of olefin
(1 mmol.) in a 1:1 mixture of t-BuOH/water (10 mL) at 0°C. The reaction
mixture was stirred at 0°C and the reaction was monitored by TLC. Upon
completion, the reaction mixture was quenched with solid Na2SO3 (1.5 g),
warmed to r.t. and stirred for an additional 60 min. The product was
extracted with ethyl acetate, washed with brine, dried over MgSO4,
concentrated and purified on silica gel. An inseparable mixture of the
required diol and the corresponding diastereomer. In order to study the
influence of the linker (PHAL, AQN, PYR) on the diastereoselection of the
reaction, various ligands were employed: - blank reaction: without ligand
- (DHQD)2-PHAL (19.48 mg, 0.025 mmol, 0.025 equiv.) - (DHQD)2-PYR (22.03
mg, 0.025 mmol, 0.025 equiv.) - (DHQD)2-AQN (21.43 mg, 0.025 mmol, 0.025
equiv.) Colourless oil. 14 (major isomer) 16 (minor isomer) 23:
(R)-5-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)-2-methylpentane-1,2-diol Colourless oil. R f =
0.53 (Pentane/ethyl acetate, 70:30). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm):
7.25 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 6.88 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 4.44 (s, 2H), 3.80
(s, 3H), 3.52-3.34 (m, 4H), 3.03 (bs, 1H), 2.59 (bs, 1H), 1.68 (m, 2H),
1.60 (m, 2H), 1.14 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm): 159.0,
129.9, 129.3, 113.6, 72.5, 72.4, 70.4, 69.4, 55.1, 35.1, 23.8, 22.9. IR
(neat) (cm-1): ν = 3387, 2935, 1611, 1512, 1463, 1245, 1032, 819, 751. MS
ESI-HRMS: m/z calc. for C14H22NaO4 + [[MNa+]: 277.1410; found: 277.1416.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Sharpless asymmetric dihydroxylation, 74% ee,
optimization study, optimized on catalytic ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Sharpless dihydroxylation reaction of chiral bishomoallylic
alcohols: Application to the synthesis of the C1-C10-C5 fragment of
FR225654
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
