$DATUM (3R,4R,5S)-3-(tert-Butoxymethyl)-5-(hydroxymethyl)-3-methyl-4-(triethylsilyloxy)-dihydro-furan-2(3H)-one
(10) To a solution of 9 (341 mg, 0.99 mmol, 1.00 eq.) in water (10.0 ml)
and tert-butanol (10.0 ml) were added (DHQD)2AQN (42.4 mg, 49.5 μmol,
5.00 mol%), potassium ferricyanide (979 mg, 2.97 mmol, 3.00 eq.) and
potassium carbonate (411 mg, 2.97 mmol, 3.00 eq.). The orange colored
reaction mixture was cooled to 0 °C. Afterwards, a solution of osmium
tetroxide (4 wt.% in water, 61.0 μl, 9.91 μmol, 1.00 mol%) was slowly
added and the reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h at 0 °C while the
color changed to yellow. The mixture was stirred for 48 h at room
temperature and quenched with sodium sulfite (1.00 g). The organic layer
was separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x
15.0 ml). The combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and
the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. Purification by flash
chromatography (20.0 g SiO2, n-hexane/ethyl acetate 10:1, 3:1).
γ-butyrolactone 10 (299 mg, 0.86 mmol, 88%, d.r. > 20:1) 3 as a colorless
oil. Rf = 0.06 (n-hexane/ethyl acetate 10:1); 1H NMR (301 MHz,
CHLOROFORM-d) δ ppm 0.64 (q, J=7.8 Hz, 6 H), 0.99 (t, J=7.8 Hz, 9 H),
1.10 (s, 3 H), 1.17 (s, 9 H), 1.87 (t, J=6.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.23 (d, J=8.5 Hz,
1 H), 3.59 (d, J=8.7 Hz, 1 H), 3.74 (ddd, J=12.2, 7.2, 4.8 Hz, 1 H), 3.99
(ddd, J=12.6, 5.9, 2.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.17 (ddd, J=7.2, 4.8, 2.5 Hz, 1 H),
4.70 (d, J=7.0 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (151 MHz, CHLOROFORM-d) δ ppm 4.9, 6.7,
14.0, 27.2, 49.3, 61.6, 63.9, 69.4, 73.4, 83.4, 178.6; HR-MS (ESI)
calculated for C17H34O5SiNa [M+Na]+: 369.2068, found: 369.2073; [α]22 D
=-7.90 ° (c = 1.00, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
