$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of the above mesylate 4 in
t-BuOH/H2O (1:1, v/v, 40 mL) were added MeSO2NH2 (362.8 mg, 3.814 mmol)
and AD-mix-β (5.3168 g), and the resultant mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 16.5 h. The reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous
Na2SO3 solution, and the resultant mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 30 min. The mixture was extracted with EtOAc, and the
organic layer was washed with 1 M aqueous NaOH solution and brine, dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthetic Studies on Amphirionin-5: Stereochemical
Assignment/Reassignment of the C1-C9 Portion through Stereodivergent
Synthesis
