$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2R,3S)-Methyl 2,3-dihydroxyoctanoate (10) To a mechanically stirred
solution of AD-mix-α (85.4 g, 1.4 g/mmol of 11) in t-BuOH: H2O (1:1, 655
mL) at 0 °C was added MeSO2NH2 (5.8 g, 0.061 mol, 1 equiv) in one
portion. After stirring at 0 °C for 2 h, to properly cool the reaction
mixture down, the liquid alkene 11 (9.6 g, 0.061 mol) was added neat via
a Pasteur pipette. The flask containing the alkene was then rinsed with
10 mL of t-BuOH/H2O solution, and this added to the reaction mixture.
Stirring was continued at 0 °C for 96 h whereupon the reaction was
quenched by adding Na2SO3 (50 g, 0.39 mol) and stirring the resultant
mixture for 1 h at rt. The mixture was then diluted with EtOAc (250 mL)
and transferred into a separatory funnel, and partitioned. The organic
layer, containing the diol 10, was separated and the aqueous phase was
further extracted with EtOAc (3 x 250 mL). The combined organic layers
were dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purification
of the crude product by SiO2 chromatography using 4:1 petrol/EtOAc as
eluent. The pure diol 10 (8.8 g, 75%) as a colorless oil. [α]D = -19.0 °
(c 1.02 CH2Cl2). IR (neat): 3389 (s), 2955 (s), 2931 (s), 2859 (m), 1742
(s), 1440 (m), 1402 (w), 1276 (m), 1217 (m), 1138 (m), 1096 (m), 1040
(m), 987 (w), 729 (w) cm-1. 1H NMR (400.11 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.08 (br dd, J =
5.6 Hz, 2.0 Hz, 1H, H5), 3.86 (br m, 1H, H6), 3.81 (s, 3H, OMe), 3.09 (d,
J = 5.2 Hz, 1H C5-OH), 1.99 (d, J = 9.2 Hz, 1H, C6-OH), 1.64-1.51
(complex m, 2H, H11ab), 1.44 (m, 2H, H12ab), 1.40-1.17 (m, 4H, H13ab,
H14ab), 0.87 (2nd order t, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H, C15-Me) ppm. 13C NMR (100.6
MHz, CDCl3) δ 174.1 (C9), 73.1 (C5), 72.5 (C6), 52.8 (OMe), 33.7 (C11),
31.6 (C13), 25.3 (C12), 22.5 (C14), 14.0 (C15) ppm. HRMS ES+: [M+Na]+
calcd for C9H18O4Na = 213.1103. Found = 213.1094.
