$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S)-N-Benzyl-2,3-dihydroxypropanamide (5) To a 250-mL round-bottomed
flask were added t-BuOH (40 mL), H2O (40 mL), and AD-mix-β (10 g, 1.4
g/mmol), and MsNH2 (0.68 g, 0.09 g/mmol). The mixture was stirred at r.t.
for ~15 min, and then cooled to 0 °C. To this cooled solution was added 4
(1.4 g, 7.1 mmol) and the mixture was stirred for 48 h at 0 °C. The
mixture was quenched with solid Na2SO3 (10.7 g) at r.t. The mixture was
diluted with EtOAc (50 mL) and, after separation of the layers, the
aqueous layer was further extracted with EtOAc (2 × 25 mL). The combined
organic layers were washed with brine (50 mL) and dried (anhyd Na2SO4).
After evaporation of the solvent, the residue was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel, EtOAc-hexane, 6:4). 5 (1.35 g, 80%) as a
white solid; 93% ee [chiral HPLC analysis: (Chiralcel OD-H, 0.46 nm i.d.
× 25 cm, n-hexane-i-PrOH, 9:1; flow rate 0.5 mL/min; UV detector: 254
nm)]. mp 81-82 °C (Lit.3g 83-84 °C); t R = 6.08 (minor, R-isomer), 8.31
min (major, S-isomer). [α]D 25 -34.3 (c 0.1, MeOH) {Lit.3g [α]D 25 -35.1
(c 0.1, MeOH)}. IR (KBr): 3406, 3296, 2924, 1629, 1536, 1427, 1243, 1071,
695 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.25-7.37 (m, 5H), 7.11 (br s,
1H), 4.48 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H), 4.18-4.25 (m, 1H), 3.82-3.98 (m, 2H),
3.40-3.48 (m, 1H), 2.63 (br s, 1H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 171.9,
137.6, 128.7, 127.6, 72.2, 64.1, 43.2. MS (ESI): m/z = 196 [M + H]+. HRMS
(ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C10H14NO3: 196.09616; found: 196.09682.
