$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Dihydroxylation of
Alkene with a Chiral Catalyst. A mixture of K3Fe(CN)6 (2.731 g, 8.36
mmol), K2CO3 (1.142 g, 8.36 mmol), and either (DHQ)2PHAL (0.108 g, 0.139
mmol, AD-mix α) or (DHQD)2PHAL (5 mol %, AD-mix β) were stirred in t-BuOH
(10 mL) and H2O (10 mL), after which OsO4 (0.7 mL, 1% aq OsO4 soln.) was
added with further stirring for 30 min at rt. CH3SO2NH2 (0.264 g, 2.78
mmol) was added and the mixture was cooled to 0 °C. Olefin 8 (0.850 g,
2.78 mmol) was added and the heterogeneous slurry was stirred vigorously
for 15 h at 0 °C and then 8 h at rt. Na2SO3 (3.2 g) was added and the
mixture was further stirred for 1 h. EtOAc (30 mL) was added and the aq
layer was extracted with EtOAc (3x20 mL). The combined organic layer was
washed with 5% KOH (2x20 mL), dried over anhyd Na2SO4, concentrated, and
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (hexanes: EtOAc=6:4) to
give the corresponding diol. Benzyl
(2S,3R)-5-[(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino]-2,3-dihydroxypentanoate as white
semisolid, yield 0.388 g, 71%. IR (KBr) 3602-3041, 1749, 1680 cm-1. 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.43 (s, 9H), 1.64-1.69 and 1.81-1.91 (2m, 2H),
2.84 (br s, 2H), 3.15-3.20 and 3.38-3.48 (2m, 2H), 4.0-4.03 (m, 1H), 4.13
(d, J=2.4 Hz, 1H), 5.26 (br s, 3H), 7.37 (s, 5H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 28.3, 34.1, 37.2, 67.6, 69.7, 73.8, 79.8, 128.3, 128.5, 128.6, 135.1,
157.0, 173.1. HRMS m/z [M + Na]+ calcd for C17H25NO6Na 362.1580, found
362.1579.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, ee=94%, Sharpless dihydroxylation
