$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of K2CO3 (52 mg, 0.38 mmol),
K3Fe(CN)6(123 mg, 0.38 mmol), K2OsO2(OH)4 (1 mg, 0.0025 mmol) and (DHQD)2
PHAL (10 mg, 0.013 mmol) in 1:1 tert-butyl alcohol-water was cooled to 0
°C. The resulting suspension was treated with the 12b (46 mg, 0.13 mmol)
and MeSO2NH2 (24 mg, 0.25 mmol), stirred at 0 °C for 16 h. The reaction
mixture quenched by addition of Na2S2O3 and extracted with ethyl acetate.
The combined organic extracts were washed with water, brine,
successively, dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo. Purification
by column chromatography (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate = 2.5:1) afforded
compound. 13a: The equivalents of K2OSO2(OH)4 and MeSO2NH2 are different
from those for dihydroxylation of 12b. Yield: 71%. [α]21D +19.0 (c 1.00,
MeOH); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.93 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 6.37 (d, J =
4.4 Hz, 1H), 6.02-6.12 (m, 1H), 5.43 (dd, J = 1.6 Hz, 17.2 Hz, 1H), 5.27
(dd, J = 1.2 Hz, 10.4 Hz, 1H), 4.52 (d, J = 5.2 Hz, 2H), 3.58 (td, J =
2.8 Hz, 10.0 Hz, 1H), 2.95 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H), 2.65-2.84 (m, 4H), 2.47
(s, 1H), 1.96-2.04 (m, 1H), 1.86 (t, 6.8 Hz, 2H), 1.77 (dd, J = 7.6 Hz,
18.0 Hz, 1H), 1.69 (dd, J = 4.0 Hz, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 1.40-1.49 (m, 1H),
1.26-1.33 (m, 8H), 1.01 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.90 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H),
0.45 (dd, J = 5.2 Hz, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 0.29-0.31 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 155.65, 152.37, 133.60, 128.29, 119.45, 116.85, 111.43, 102.58,
87.48, 79.15, 72.68, 68.69, 34.54, 33.36, 32.71, 32.30, 29.96, 28.17,
26.02, 25.98, 23.75, 20.09, 19.92, 18.42, 12.12; HRMS (ESIMS) calculated
for C25H36O4Na [M + Na]+ 423.2506, found 423.2502.
