$DATUM (2R,3R)-3-Methoxy-5-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)pentane-1,2-diol (21) AD-mix-α
(67.1 g, 45.0 mmol) and MeSO2NH2 (4.2 g, 45.0 mmol) were added to 20 (10
g, 45.0 mmol) in t-BuOH (109 mL) and H2O (109 mL) at 0 °C. The reaction
mixture was stirred at the same temperature for 3 d and quenched by the
addition of sat. aq Na2SO3 (40 mL) and 1 M aq KOH (35 mL). After 10 min,
the mixture was warmed to r.t. and stirred for an additional 30 min. The
reaction contents were transferred to a separatory funnel with EtOAc (75
mL), the phases were separated and the aqueous layer was further
extracted with EtOAc (4 × 250 mL). The combined organic layer was dried
(Na2SO4) and concentrated in vacuo and the residue was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel, EtOAc-hexanes, 5:5); This afforded the diol
compound 21. Yield: 9.9 g (36.6 mmol, 82%); >95% diastereoselectivity as
determined by chiral HPLC; viscous liquid; [α]D 25 -2.9 (c 0.85, CHCl3).
IR (neat): 3410, 2930, 1613, 1513, 1324, 1246, 1085, 1032, 820, 764, 523
cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ = 7.25 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2 H), 6.88 (d, J
= 8.3 Hz, 2 H), 4.92 (bs, 1 H), 4.44 (s, 2 H), 3.81 (s, 3 H), 3.76- 3.48
(m, 5 H), 3.45-3.30 (m, 4 H), 2.01-1.78 (m, 2 H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75
MHz): δ = 159.1, 129.8, 129.3, 113.7, 79.4, 72.9, 72.3, 65.8, 63.9, 58.0,
55.2, 30.1. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd for C14H22O5Na [M + Na]+: 293.1357;
found: 293.1359.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The first total synthesis of pectinolide F
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
